_README_TEMPLATE = '''# {pkg_name}

An engram-package — a portable, read-only ENGRAM knowledge graph that other agents can clone and consume alongside their personal graph.

## What this package contains

- `knowledge.sql` — source of truth, versioned in git
- `knowledge.db` — build artifact, gitignored, regenerated via `scripts/build.sh`
- `scripts/dump.sh` — author-side: writes `knowledge.sql` from live `knowledge.db`
- `scripts/build.sh` — consumer-side: rebuilds `knowledge.db` from `knowledge.sql`
- (optional) `cases/`, `archive/`, etc. — domain-specific human-readable content

## Consumer workflow

```bash
git clone <this-repo>
cd <this-repo>
bash scripts/build.sh    # produces knowledge.db
```

You can then query the package via the engram-pkg CLI:

```bash
